-- title:
--   Smooth neighbourhood of a good point of the integral model
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a field $k$ the symbol $k((q))$ denotes `LaurentSeries k`. A *place* of $F$ over $K$ (for $K \subseteq F$ fields) is, in the sense used here, a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, all of whose ideals are principal; `Place.ord` is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation, and `Place.evalAt` sends an element of the valuation subring to the preimage in $K$ of its residue (and sends elements outside the valuation subring to $0$).
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$; a valuation subring $A \subseteq \bar{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Two intermediate fields of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the field generated over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, and `fieldBar q M'`, generated over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   **Supersingular places.** A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` — the subfield of $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)((q))$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'` — over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, with `hW` asserting that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the places $w$ that are rational (i.e. $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ surjects onto the residue field of $w$), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen …)` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of $j$ with the property that every elliptic Weierstrass curve of that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **Constant reduction.** A datum $R_0$ of type `ConstantReduction A (modularFunctionFieldBar M') (modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M')`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` meeting $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the geometric modular function field over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with reduction in $A$, the scaling property that every nonzero element becomes, after multiplication by a suitable constant, an integral element with nonzero residue, together with a degree-preserving map on places and the compatibility of divisor pushforward with orders of residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, viewed in $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)((q))$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Igusa family.** An element $\zeta$ of `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$) and a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), the projective line over $\mathbb Z/q$, subject to: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ as a Gauss ring, namely $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$; `hIg`, that every point of the projective line is of the form $\overline{\gamma} \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\overline{\gamma} =$ `redQ q γ`, the corresponding ring being the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` (the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` singled out by `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, the identity if none exists); `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every $\zeta'$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family, by a permutation of the projective line.
--
--   **Supersingular family.** A family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$, subject to four hypotheses. `hSS_A`: for $x \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ iff $x \in A$. `hSS_over`: for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $j$ given by the coefficientwise image of `jq` has nonnegative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the images of $f$ and $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix`: each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: for each $s \in W$ there is $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that for every $a \in A$ the difference $t - a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   **Regular prolongation.** A datum $R$ of type `RegularProlongation A (fieldBar q M') (xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M'))` — a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` meeting $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, with surjective residue map onto the indicated function field over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with reduction in $A$, and the scaling property — with `hR` identifying `R.integers` with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, and `hR₀O` stating that an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   **Uniformisers and the small field $k_0$.** An element $\pi \in \bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$. An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A \cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ to $k_0$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and roots of unity.** A prime number $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **The finite layer.** An intermediate field $K_1$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, finite over $k_0$, and a valuation subring $A_1 \subseteq K_1$ with $x \in A_1$ iff $x \in A$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, with `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is the following. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ such that: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ finite over $k_0$, every family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum $T' := k_0(\text{image of } K') \sqcup F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ has all $a_i = 0$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb` (that is, has rational coefficients) lies in $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the image of $K_1$. Let $T_1$ carry an $A_1$-algebra structure whose structure map agrees with the inclusion of $K_1$ into `fieldBar q M'` through $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, and let $j_1 \in T_1$ be an element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by the coefficientwise image of `jq`, with $j_1 \neq 0$. Let $\mathfrak X_1 :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two maps from the middle chart to $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1]$ in $T_1$ and $X_\infty = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure of $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$.
--
--   A point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ is called *good* when the five following conditions hold: (i) `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; (ii) the only point $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ is $x$ itself, i.e. $x$ is a closed point; (iii) for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `ιFin` $y = x$, every element $b$ of the chart algebra of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in the prime ideal of $y$; (iv) the same with $X_\infty$, `ιInf` and the chart algebra of $X_\infty$; (v) for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with `ιFin` $y = x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime ideal of $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7).
--
--   The conclusion: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ that is good in this sense, there exists an open subscheme $U$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ such that $x \in U$ and the composite of the open immersion $U \to \mathfrak X_1$ followed by `toBase` is a smooth morphism.
--
--   This is the per-point smoothness statement for the two-chart integral model of the full-level modular curve over the henselian discrete valuation ring $A_1$: a closed point of the special fibre lying on the branch cut out by the Gauss (Igusa) valuation ring `R.integers` and not lying over a supersingular $j$-invariant has a neighbourhood smooth over the base. It is obtained by transporting the corresponding statement for the two-chart model attached to `xHFunctionField` along the coefficientwise identification of level fields and the functoriality of the two-chart model in the field, and it is used in the descent form of the same result and in the construction of étale coordinates at off-branch points.
